001-msvc-1952-has-include-next.patch
================================================================================
WHAT IT FIXES
  include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h line 35 reads

      #if defined(__clang__) && __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)

  MSVC 19.51 (the 2026-08-29 Windows builds) let the false defined(__clang__)
  short-circuit the undefined __has_include_next(...) with warning C4067, which
  the header disables. MSVC 19.52 (Visual Studio 2026 18.12, toolset
  14.52.37025, first used 2026-11-18) makes it a hard error:

      error C7780: function-like macro '__has_include_next' is not defined
      fatal error C1017: invalid integer constant expression

  so every dav1d source that includes <stdatomic.h> fails to compile for
  win-x64. The patch nests the clang-only test so that cl never evaluates
  __has_include_next, and selects exactly the same branch as upstream on every
  compiler: cl -> the header's own Interlocked* atomics (unchanged); clang-cl
  (win-arm64) -> clang's <stdatomic.h> through #include_next (unchanged).

WHICH PLATFORMS IT AFFECTS
  Windows only. meson.build adds include/compat/msvc to the include path only
  when cc.get_id() == 'msvc', so the patched header is never compiled on Linux,
  macOS or Android. Those scripts still apply the patch to their scratch copy
  (they apply every patch in this folder) and record it in BUILD-INFO; their
  object code is unaffected.

UPSTREAM
  Not reported upstream as of 2026-11-18. The header is unchanged at the
  vendored commit 52b9d3d3 (1.5.4-1).

WHEN IT CAN BE DROPPED
  When the vendored snapshot is bumped to a dav1d whose
  include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h no longer evaluates __has_include_next in an
  #if that cl reads. Re-check by building win-x64 without this patch.

APPLIES WITH
  git apply -p1 (windows/build-common.ps1, against the CRLF working copy) and
  patch -p1 --forward --batch (linux/, macos/, against LF); both verified on
  2026-11-18. Everything above the "diff --git" line is ignored by both tools.
================================================================================

diff --git a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
index 618f0ee..57d53bd 100644
--- a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
+++ b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
@@ -32,7 +32,14 @@
 #pragma warning(push)
 #pragma warning(disable:4067)    /* newline for __has_include_next */
 
-#if defined(__clang__) && __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)
+/* CodeBrix patch 001: MSVC 19.52 rejects an undefined function-like macro in #if even
+ * behind a false '&&', so the clang-only test is nested. Same branches as upstream. */
+#if defined(__clang__)
+#  if __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)
+#    define DAV1D_MSVC_COMPAT_USE_CLANG_STDATOMIC 1
+#  endif
+#endif
+#if defined(DAV1D_MSVC_COMPAT_USE_CLANG_STDATOMIC)
    /* use the clang stdatomic.h with clang-cl*/
 #  include_next <stdatomic.h>
 #else /* ! stdatomic.h */
